# Cursor & AI Instructions for MatchPulse

## Project Context
MatchPulse is an AI-powered cricket explainer app built with Next.js 14 App Router, TypeScript, and Google Gemini 2.0 Flash. It translates match tension into plain Hinglish/English cards in under 5 seconds.

## Code Style & Standards
- Strict TypeScript: no 'any' types anywhere
- Functional React components with hooks, wrapped in React.memo where appropriate
- Pure functions for cricket math in lib/cricket.ts
- Zod schemas for all runtime validations at API boundaries
- Mobile-first dark UI styling with pitch-green (#00d26a) accent

## Architectural Patterns
- API route pipeline: Validate input (Zod) → Fast-path check (completed match) → Compute deterministic stats → Call AI → Validate schema → Return JSON
- Deterministic ground truth: Never let AI calculate RRR or balls remaining; compute them in pure functions first
- Error resilience: Return structured errors (400, 429, 500) and graceful mock fallbacks when API keys are absent

## Testing
- Unit and property-based tests in Vitest with fast-check (1000 runs)
- E2E tests with Playwright
